IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-dates`

-- Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) -- the rules: Part IA (the Court), Part I (investments), Part II (general powers, indemnities,
-- maintenance, advancement and protective trusts), Part III (appointment and discharge of trustees), Part IV (powers of
-- the Court: appointing trustees, vesting orders, dealings, variation, relief, impounding, payment into court) and
-- s 77 (commission), so far as they give a beneficiary a fact test.
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in ta-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("shall not", "is not liable",
-- "means", "unless", "if" and "where" conditions that fail, a period the text fixes); or NOTHING where the Act does not
-- answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The Court's judgments ("expedient", "honestly and
-- reasonably", "ought fairly to be excused", "for the benefit of") and the trustee's ("reasonably believes", "prudent")
-- are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- s 2(3): the Act's powers, discretions, duties and directions apply "unless otherwise stated ... if and so far only as a
-- contrary intention is not expressed in the instrument (if any) creating the trust". Where a question turns on that, a
-- contrary intention answers JUST FALSE (fork F3 in NOTES.md).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Trustee Act
-- 1958, Version No. 127 (1 September 2023), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
-- authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the
-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Trustee Act 1958`

§§ `Part IA -- the Court (s 3)`

-- s 3(1): "Court means the Supreme Court and, in relation to property or an estate or interest in property the value of
-- which property does not exceed the jurisdictional limit of the County Court, the Supreme Court or the County Court".
-- The County Court's jurisdictional limit is set by the County Court Act 1958 (borrowed: asked as a fact).
DECLARE `The Court for my trust` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court only`
    `the Supreme Court or the County Court`

GIVEN `the value does not exceed the County Court limit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Court for my trust`
`s 3 -- the Court` `the value does not exceed the County Court limit` MEANS
    IF `the value does not exceed the County Court limit`
    THEN `the Supreme Court or the County Court`
    ELSE `the Supreme Court only`

§§ `Part I -- investments (ss 5 to 12E)`

-- s 5: "A trustee may, unless expressly prohibited by the instrument creating the trust -- (a) invest trust funds in any
-- form of investment; and (b) at any time, vary an investment." Expressly prohibited: JUST FALSE ("unless").
GIVEN `the instrument expressly prohibits it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5 -- the trustee may invest in it` `the instrument expressly prohibits it` MEANS
    IF `the instrument expressly prohibits it`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 6(1): "Subject to the instrument creating the trust, a trustee must, in exercising a power of investment -- (a) if
-- the trustee's profession, business or employment is or includes acting as a trustee or investing money on behalf of
-- other persons, exercise the care, diligence and skill that a prudent person engaged in that profession, business or
-- employment would exercise in managing the affairs of other persons; or (b) if the trustee is not engaged in such a
-- profession, business or employment, exercise the care, diligence and skill that a prudent person would exercise in
-- managing the affairs of other persons."
-- The instrument sets its own standard: NOTHING-kind *points outside the text* (the instrument governs).
DECLARE `Standard of care in investing` IS ONE OF
    `that of a prudent person engaged in the profession, business or employment of acting as a trustee or investing for others`
    `that of a prudent person managing the affairs of other persons`

GIVEN `the trustee's work includes acting as trustee or investing for others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument sets another standard`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Standard of care in investing`
`s 6(1) -- the standard of care` `the trustee's work includes acting as trustee or investing for others` `the instrument sets another standard` MEANS
    IF `the instrument sets another standard`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the trustee's work includes acting as trustee or investing for others`
         THEN JUST `that of a prudent person engaged in the profession, business or employment of acting as a trustee or investing for others`
         ELSE JUST `that of a prudent person managing the affairs of other persons`

-- s 6(2): "A trustee must exercise a power of investment in accordance with any provision of the instrument creating the
-- trust that is binding on the trustee and requires the obtaining of any consent or approval with respect to trust
-- investments." No such provision: NOTHING-kind *silent*.
GIVEN `the instrument requires a consent or approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision binds the trustee`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) -- the trustee must obtain the consent` `the instrument requires a consent or approval` `the provision binds the trustee` MEANS
    IF `the instrument requires a consent or approval` AND `the provision binds the trustee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 8(1): "a trustee must, so far as they are appropriate to the circumstances of the trust, have regard to -- (a) ... (o)".
DECLARE `Investment matter` IS ONE OF
    `(a) the purposes of the trust and the needs and circumstances of the beneficiaries`
    `(b) the desirability of diversifying trust investments`
    `(c) the nature of and risk associated with existing trust investments and other trust property`
    `(d) the need to maintain the real value of the capital or income of the trust`
    `(e) the risk of capital or income loss or depreciation`
    `(f) the potential for capital appreciation`
    `(g) the likely income return and the timing of income return`
    `(h) the length of the term of the proposed investment`
    `(i) the probable duration of the trust`
    `(j) the liquidity and marketability of the proposed investment`
    `(k) the aggregate value of the trust estate`
    `(l) the effect of the proposed investment on the tax liability of the trust`
    `(m) the likelihood of inflation affecting the value of the proposed investment or other trust property`
    `(n) the costs of making the proposed investment`
    `(o) the results of a review of existing trust investments`

-- Every matter is on the list, so the matter itself decides nothing; whether it is "appropriate to the circumstances of
-- the trust" does. Not appropriate: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* ("so far as", no "only").
GIVEN `the matter`                  IS AN `Investment matter`
      `it is appropriate to the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) -- the trustee must have regard to the matter` `the matter` `it is appropriate to the trust` MEANS
    IF `it is appropriate to the trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 8(2): "A trustee may -- (a) obtain and consider independent and impartial advice reasonably required for the
-- investment of trust funds or the management of the investment from a person whom the trustee reasonably believes to be
-- competent to give the advice; and (b) pay out of trust funds the reasonable costs of obtaining the advice."
-- s 7(4): "If a trustee is under a duty to take advice, the reasonable costs of obtaining the advice are payable out of
-- trust funds." (Whether the general law puts the trustee under a duty to take this advice (s 7(2)(d)) is borrowed:
-- asked.) Costs not reasonable, or the advice outside both: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*.
GIVEN `the trustee was under a duty to take the advice`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advice is independent and impartial`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advice was reasonably required for the investment`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee reasonably believes the adviser competent`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are reasonable`                               IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 7(4), 8(2) -- the advice may be paid for out of trust funds` `the trustee was under a duty to take the advice` `the advice is independent and impartial` `the advice was reasonably required for the investment` `the trustee reasonably believes the adviser competent` `the costs are reasonable` MEANS
    IF `the costs are reasonable`
       AND (    `the trustee was under a duty to take the advice`
            OR (`the advice is independent and impartial` AND `the advice was reasonably required for the investment` AND `the trustee reasonably believes the adviser competent`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 11(1): "Subject to the instrument creating the trust, a trustee may -- (a) invest any trust funds in the purchase of
-- a dwelling house for a beneficiary to use as a residence; or (b) enter into any other agreement or arrangement to
-- secure for a beneficiary a right to use a dwelling house as a residence." (2): "Despite the terms of the instrument
-- creating the trust, a trustee may, if to do so would not unfairly prejudice the interests of the other beneficiaries,
-- retain as part of the trust property a dwelling house for a beneficiary to use as a residence."
-- (1) with an instrument that forbids it: JUST FALSE (fork F4); (2) with unfair prejudice: JUST FALSE ("if").
DECLARE `Home for a beneficiary` IS ONE OF
    `buying a dwelling house for me to live in`
    `another arrangement giving me a right to live in a dwelling house`
    `keeping a dwelling house the trust already holds, for me to live in`

GIVEN `the arrangement`                                  IS A `Home for a beneficiary`
      `the instrument forbids it`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would unfairly prejudice the other beneficiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11 -- the trustee may provide the home` `the arrangement` `the instrument forbids it` `it would unfairly prejudice the other beneficiaries` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the arrangement`
    WHEN `keeping a dwelling house the trust already holds, for me to live in` THEN
        IF `it would unfairly prejudice the other beneficiaries`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the instrument forbids it`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 12: "A trustee is not liable for breach of trust by reason only of retaining an investment that has ceased to be --
-- (a) an investment authorised by the instrument ...; (b) an investment properly made ...; (c) ... under this Act ...;
-- (d) ... authorised by any other Act or the general law." The complaint is more than the retaining: NOTHING-kind
-- *limited by its own wording* ("by reason only").
GIVEN `the investment has ceased to be authorised or proper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only complaint is that it was kept`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 -- the trustee is liable for keeping the investment` `the investment has ceased to be authorised or proper` `the only complaint is that it was kept` MEANS
    IF `the investment has ceased to be authorised or proper` AND `the only complaint is that it was kept`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 12A(1): "If a trustee lends money on the security of property, the trustee is not liable for breach of trust by
-- reason only of the proportion borne by the amount of the loan to the value of the property ... if it appears to the
-- Court -- (a) that, in making the loan, the trustee was acting on a report as to the value of the property made by a
-- person whom the trustee reasonably believed to be competent ... and whom the trustee instructed and employed
-- independently of any owner of the property; and (b) that the amount of the loan did not exceed two-thirds of the value
-- of the property as stated in the report; and (c) that the loan was made in reliance on the report."
-- JUST TRUE: s 12A protects; JUST FALSE: "this section gives no protection on these facts" ("if").
GIVEN `the loan`                                        IS A NUMBER
      `the value in the report`                         IS A NUMBER
      `the trustee acted on a valuation report`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee reasonably believed the valuer competent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the valuer was instructed independently of any owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loan was made in reliance on the report`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A -- the trustee is protected as to the proportion lent` `the loan` `the value in the report` `the trustee acted on a valuation report` `the trustee reasonably believed the valuer competent` `the valuer was instructed independently of any owner` `the loan was made in reliance on the report` MEANS
    IF     `the trustee acted on a valuation report`
       AND `the trustee reasonably believed the valuer competent`
       AND `the valuer was instructed independently of any owner`
       AND (`the loan` TIMES 3) AT MOST (`the value in the report` TIMES 2)
       AND `the loan was made in reliance on the report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 12B(1): "If a trustee improperly advances trust money on a security that would at the time of the investment have
-- been a proper investment if the sum advanced had been smaller than the actual sum advanced, the security is to be taken
-- to be a proper investment in respect of the smaller sum, and the trustee is only liable to make good the difference
-- between the sum advanced and the smaller sum, with interest." The rate of interest is not stated: the interest is an
-- input (finding 4). Not that case (the smaller sum is not smaller): NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*.
GIVEN `the sum advanced`          IS A NUMBER
      `the smaller proper sum`    IS A NUMBER
      `the interest on the difference` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 12B -- the most the trustee must make good` `the sum advanced` `the smaller proper sum` `the interest on the difference` MEANS
    IF `the smaller proper sum` LESS THAN `the sum advanced`
    THEN JUST ((`the sum advanced` MINUS `the smaller proper sum`) PLUS `the interest on the difference`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 12D(1): "The Court may, when considering an action for breach of trust arising out of or in respect of an investment
-- by a trustee where a loss has been, or is expected to be, sustained by the trust, set off all or part of the loss
-- resulting from that investment against all or part of the gain resulting from any other investment whether in breach of
-- trust or not." No loss, or no such action: JUST FALSE ("when", "where": rulings (b), (c)).
GIVEN `it is an action for breach of trust over an investment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a loss has been or is expected to be sustained`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D -- the Court may set off gains against the loss` `it is an action for breach of trust over an investment` `a loss has been or is expected to be sustained` MEANS
    IF `it is an action for breach of trust over an investment` AND `a loss has been or is expected to be sustained`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 12E(6): "housing loan means a loan -- (a) made for any one or more of the following purposes, that is to say, of
-- enabling the borrower -- (i) ... (vi) ...; and (b) the repayment of which is secured by security over the interest of
-- the borrower in the land". "Prescribed interest in land" (fee simple or a Crown or other lease giving reasonable
-- security) is asked as part of the purpose.
DECLARE `Purpose of the loan` IS ONE OF
    `(i) to acquire a prescribed interest in land and build or finish a dwelling-house on it`
    `(ii) to build or finish a dwelling-house on land the borrower has a prescribed interest in`
    `(iii) to acquire a prescribed interest in land with a dwelling-house on it`
    `(iv) to alter, improve or extend a dwelling-house on land the borrower has a prescribed interest in`
    `(v) to pay for roads, kerbing, guttering or footpaths for land the borrower has a prescribed interest in`
    `(vi) to discharge a mortgage over land with a prescribed interest on which a dwelling-house is being built`
    `none of these purposes`

GIVEN `the purpose`                              IS A `Purpose of the loan`
      `secured over the borrower's interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12E(6) -- the loan is a housing loan` `the purpose` `secured over the borrower's interest in the land` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `none of these purposes` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `secured over the borrower's interest in the land`

-- s 12E(1): "If a trustee lends money on a real security in accordance with the provisions of this Act ..., the trustee is
-- not chargeable with breach of trust by reason only of the proportion borne by the amount of the loan to the value of
-- the property on which the loan is secured if -- (a) the trustee was not expressly forbidden by the instrument (if any)
-- creating the trust to lend money on a real security; and (b) the loan was a housing loan; and (c) the loan is secured by
-- a contract of insurance in the prescribed form entered into with an authorised insurer." JUST FALSE: "this section
-- gives no protection on these facts" ("if").
GIVEN `the trustee was expressly forbidden to lend on real security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose`                                                IS A `Purpose of the loan`
      `secured over the borrower's interest in the land`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `insured in the prescribed form with an authorised insurer`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12E -- the trustee is protected as to the proportion lent on a housing loan` `the trustee was expressly forbidden to lend on real security` `the purpose` `secured over the borrower's interest in the land` `insured in the prescribed form with an authorised insurer` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `the trustee was expressly forbidden to lend on real security`)
       AND `s 12E(6) -- the loan is a housing loan` `the purpose` `secured over the borrower's interest in the land`
       AND `insured in the prescribed form with an authorised insurer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part II Division 1 -- sale, mortgage, insurance (ss 14 to 17, 23)`

-- s 14(1): "Where the instrument creating a power to sell property does not expressly limit the duration of the power,
-- then, notwithstanding any lapse of time or that all the beneficiaries are absolutely entitled ... the trustee may, if so
-- requested in writing by any beneficiary, sell the property". No power, or a limited duration: JUST FALSE ("where");
-- no written request: JUST FALSE ("if"). JUST TRUE: s 14 lets the trustee sell; it never obliges it to (fork F5).
GIVEN `there is a power to sell the property`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument expressly limits how long it lasts`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `a beneficiary has asked in writing`                 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14 -- the trustee may sell at a beneficiary's written request` `there is a power to sell the property` `the instrument expressly limits how long it lasts` `a beneficiary has asked in writing` MEANS
    IF `there is a power to sell the property` AND (NOT `the instrument expressly limits how long it lasts`) AND `a beneficiary has asked in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 15(1): "No sale made by a trustee shall be impeached by any beneficiary upon the ground that any of the conditions
-- subject to which the sale was made may have been unnecessarily depreciatory unless it also appears that the
-- consideration for the sale was thereby rendered inadequate." (2): "No sale ... shall, after the execution of the
-- conveyance, be impeached as against the purchaser upon the ground that any of the conditions ... may have been
-- unnecessarily depreciatory, unless it appears that the purchaser was acting in collusion with the trustee at the time
-- when the contract of sale was made."
-- Not that ground: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*. Barred: JUST FALSE. Not barred: JUST TRUE (s 15 merely
-- stops barring; fork F6).
GIVEN `the conditions were unnecessarily depreciatory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price was made inadequate by them`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance has been executed`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser colluded with the trustee`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- the sale may be impeached for depreciatory conditions` `the conditions were unnecessarily depreciatory` `the price was made inadequate by them` `the conveyance has been executed` `the purchaser colluded with the trustee` MEANS
    IF NOT `the conditions were unnecessarily depreciatory`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT `the price was made inadequate by them`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the conveyance has been executed` AND (NOT `the purchaser colluded with the trustee`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 16(1): on a sale of land in fee simple "the trustees ... may, where the proceeds are liable to be invested, contract
-- that the payment of any part, not exceeding three-fifths, of the purchase money shall be secured by a mortgage of the
-- land sold". (3): under an order of the Court, "only if and so far as the Court may by order direct".
-- Over three-fifths: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* (the grant stops at three-fifths). Proceeds not to be
-- invested: JUST FALSE ("where"). A sale under a Court order without the Court's direction: JUST FALSE ("only if").
GIVEN `the price`                                IS A NUMBER
      `the part to be secured by mortgage`       IS A NUMBER
      `the proceeds are liable to be invested`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is under an order of the Court`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed it`                IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16 -- the trustee may leave part of the price on mortgage` `the price` `the part to be secured by mortgage` `the proceeds are liable to be invested` `the sale is under an order of the Court` `the Court has directed it` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceeds are liable to be invested`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the sale is under an order of the Court` AND (NOT `the Court has directed it`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF (`the part to be secured by mortgage` TIMES 5) AT MOST (`the price` TIMES 3)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING

-- s 17(3): the terms of a sale of land on deferred payment "shall ... include provisions for giving effect to the
-- following -- (a) that the part of the purchase money to be paid by way of deposit shall not be less than the sum which
-- a person acting with prudence would, if the land were his own, have accepted ..., and in any case shall not be less
-- than one-tenth of the purchase money; (b) that the balance ... shall bear interest payable half-yearly or oftener ...,
-- and in any case the whole purchase-money shall be payable within a period not exceeding ten years from the date of
-- sale; (c) that if any instalment or interest or part thereof is in arrear and unpaid for six months, or for such less
-- period as may be specified, the whole of the purchase money shall become due and payable; (d) that the purchaser shall
-- maintain and protect the property, and keep all buildings (if any) thereon insured against loss or damage by fire to
-- the full insurable value thereof." (5): under a Court order, "unless the Court otherwise directs".
-- Terms short of any of these: JUST FALSE (a "shall" not met, fork F7).
GIVEN `the price`                                 IS A NUMBER
      `the deposit`                               IS A NUMBER
      `the deposit a prudent owner would accept`  IS A NUMBER
      `the months between interest payments`      IS A NUMBER
      `the years until the whole price is due`    IS A NUMBER
      `the months of arrears before the whole price falls due` IS A NUMBER
      `the purchaser must maintain and insure against fire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17(3) -- the deferred payment terms meet the minimums` `the price` `the deposit` `the deposit a prudent owner would accept` `the months between interest payments` `the years until the whole price is due` `the months of arrears before the whole price falls due` `the purchaser must maintain and insure against fire` IF
        `the deposit` AT LEAST `the deposit a prudent owner would accept`
    AND (`the deposit` TIMES 10) AT LEAST `the price`
    AND `the months between interest payments` AT MOST 6
    AND `the years until the whole price is due` AT MOST 10
    AND `the months of arrears before the whole price falls due` AT MOST 6
    AND `the purchaser must maintain and insure against fire`

-- s 17(4)(a): "Notwithstanding that the land has been sold on terms of deferred payment, the trustee may at any time after
-- two-fifths of the purchase money has been paid convey the land and take a mortgage back to secure payment of the
-- balance". Before two-fifths is paid: JUST FALSE (a period the text fixes, ruling (a); fork F8 on "after").
GIVEN `the price`     IS A NUMBER
      `the part paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(4) -- the trustee may convey and take a mortgage back` `the price` `the part paid` MEANS
    IF (`the part paid` TIMES 5) AT LEAST (`the price` TIMES 2)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 23(1): "A trustee may insure against loss or damage, whether by fire or otherwise, any insurable property, and against
-- any risk or liability against which it would be prudent for a person to insure if he were acting for himself." (2):
-- "The insurance may be for any amount: Provided that together with the amount of any insurance already on foot the total
-- shall not exceed the insurable value or liability." Over: JUST FALSE ("shall not").
GIVEN `the amount of the new insurance`       IS A NUMBER
      `the insurance already on foot`         IS A NUMBER
      `the insurable value or liability`      IS A NUMBER
      `a prudent person would insure against it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23 -- the trustee may insure for the amount` `the amount of the new insurance` `the insurance already on foot` `the insurable value or liability` `a prudent person would insure against it` MEANS
    IF NOT `a prudent person would insure against it`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (`the amount of the new insurance` PLUS `the insurance already on foot`) AT MOST `the insurable value or liability`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part II Divisions 1 and 2 -- whether the trustee answers for a loss (ss 28, 36)`

DECLARE `Cause of the loss` IS ONE OF
    `my trustee's own act, receipt, neglect or default`
    `another trustee's act, receipt, neglect or default`
    `a banker, broker or other person with whom trust money or securities were deposited`
    `an agent my trustee employed`
    `the insufficiency or deficiency of securities`
    `money or securities my trustee signed a receipt for only for conformity and did not receive`
    `some other cause`

-- s 36(1): "A trustee shall be chargeable only for money and securities actually received by him notwithstanding his
-- signing any receipt for the sake of conformity, and shall be answerable and accountable only for his own acts,
-- receipts, neglects or defaults, and not for those of any other trustee, nor for any banker, broker or other person with
-- whom any trust money or securities may be deposited, nor for the insufficiency or deficiency of any securities, nor for
-- any other loss unless the same happens through his own wilful default."
-- s 28(1): trustees "shall not be responsible for the default of any such agent if employed in good faith".
-- JUST TRUE: the section shields the trustee. Own acts: JUST FALSE (the shield's "only" leaves them out). An agent not
-- employed in good faith: JUST FALSE ("if"). Wilful default: JUST FALSE ("unless"), read across every head (fork F9).
GIVEN `the cause`                               IS A `Cause of the loss`
      `it happened through my trustee's own wilful default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent was employed in good faith`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 28, 36 -- the trustee is shielded from the loss` `the cause` `it happened through my trustee's own wilful default` `the agent was employed in good faith` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `my trustee's own act, receipt, neglect or default` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an agent my trustee employed` THEN
        IF `the agent was employed in good faith` AND (NOT `it happened through my trustee's own wilful default`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `it happened through my trustee's own wilful default`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part II Division 1 -- appropriation to a beneficiary's share (s 31)`

-- s 31(5), (6), (13): the beneficiary's interest. s 31(13): "settled legacy share or interest means -- (a) a legacy share
-- or interest settled by the trust instrument ...; (b) an annuity ...; and (c) any legacy share or interest to which at
-- the time of appropriation no person is absolutely and beneficially entitled in possession."
DECLARE `My interest in the share` IS ONE OF
    `I am absolutely and beneficially entitled to it in possession`
    `it is a settled share and I am entitled to its income`
    `it is a fund set apart to pay my annuity`

-- s 31(7): "If the person ... (a) is a minor ... (b) is incompetent to manage his own affairs or incapable of managing his
-- own affairs ... (c) is a person whom the trustee has been unable at the time of the appropriation to find or who cannot
-- be ascertained, or as to whom it is uncertain at that time whether he is living or dead".
DECLARE `My standing for consent` IS ONE OF
    `I am of full age and capacity`
    `I am a minor`
    `I am incapable of managing my own affairs`
    `the trustee cannot find me or does not know whether I am alive`

DECLARE `Who may consent` IS ONE OF
    `I may, in writing`
    `the separate trustee of my share may, in writing`
    `my parent with whom I live or who has custody of me, or my guardian`
    `a person with power by law to consent for me`
    `the Court`

-- s 31(9): "where a fund is set apart to answer an annuity (not being an annuity in respect of which the trustee is liable
-- to pay or provide, in addition to the annuity, any moneys by way of tax or otherwise) ..., the consent of the annuitant
-- shall not be necessary if -- (a) the fund at the time of appropriation would be sufficient, if it were invested in
-- securities of the Government of the Commonwealth of Australia at par, to provide an income exceeding the annuity by at
-- least twenty per centum thereof; and (b) the fund is actually invested in such securities."
GIVEN `the yearly annuity`                                IS A NUMBER
      `the yearly income at par in Commonwealth securities` IS A NUMBER
      `the fund is actually so invested`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee must also pay tax or other moneys`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(9) -- the annuitant's consent is not necessary` `the yearly annuity` `the yearly income at par in Commonwealth securities` `the fund is actually so invested` `the trustee must also pay tax or other moneys` IF
        (NOT `the trustee must also pay tax or other moneys`)
    AND (`the yearly income at par in Commonwealth securities` TIMES 5) AT LEAST (`the yearly annuity` TIMES 6)
    AND `the fund is actually so invested`

-- s 31(5): absolute share: no appropriation "unless, if that person is of full age and capacity he consents in writing,
-- or if he is not ..., consent is given as provided by subsection (7)". (6): settled share: "unless consent in writing
-- thereto is given -- (a) by the trustee thereof (if any) not being also the trustee making the appropriation; or (b) by
-- the person for the time being entitled to the income provided he is of full age and capacity; or (c) in the manner
-- provided in subsection (7)". (8): "If the appropriation is of an investment authorized by law, or by the instrument
-- ..., no consent shall be required -- (a) on behalf of a minor, where there is no parent or guardian; (b) on behalf of a
-- person who is incompetent ..., where there is no person having power by the law to give the consent; or (c) on behalf
-- of a person whom the trustee has been unable ... to find ... -- save that if there is a trustee of the legacy share or
-- interest his consent shall be required."
-- JUST TRUE: a consent for my share is needed; JUST FALSE: none (s 31(8), (9): "no consent shall be required", "shall
-- not be necessary").
GIVEN `my interest`                                       IS A `My interest in the share`
      `my standing`                                       IS A `My standing for consent`
      `I have a parent or guardian`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone has power by law to consent for me`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an investment authorised by law or the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a separate trustee of my share`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the annuity fund meets section 31(9)`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31 -- a consent for my share is needed` `my interest` `my standing` `I have a parent or guardian` `someone has power by law to consent for me` `it is an investment authorised by law or the instrument` `there is a separate trustee of my share` `the annuity fund meets section 31(9)` MEANS
    IF `the annuity fund meets section 31(9)` AND `my interest` EQUALS `it is a fund set apart to pay my annuity`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it is an investment authorised by law or the instrument` AND `there is no one to consent on my behalf`
         THEN IF `there is a separate trustee of my share`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `there is no one to consent on my behalf` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my standing`
            WHEN `I am a minor` THEN NOT `I have a parent or guardian`
            WHEN `I am incapable of managing my own affairs` THEN NOT `someone has power by law to consent for me`
            WHEN `the trustee cannot find me or does not know whether I am alive` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Who may give the consent (s 31(5), (6), (7)). A separate trustee of a settled share or annuity fund comes first (s
-- 31(6)(a)); then the beneficiary in writing if of full age and capacity, or those (7) names.
GIVEN `my interest`                         IS A `My interest in the share`
      `my standing`                         IS A `My standing for consent`
      `there is a separate trustee of my share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Who may consent`
`s 31 -- who may consent for my share` `my interest` `my standing` `there is a separate trustee of my share` MEANS
    IF `there is a separate trustee of my share` AND (NOT (`my interest` EQUALS `I am absolutely and beneficially entitled to it in possession`))
    THEN `the separate trustee of my share may, in writing` FOLLOWED BY `for me`
    ELSE `for me`
    WHERE
        `for me` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my standing`
            WHEN `I am of full age and capacity` THEN LIST `I may, in writing`
            WHEN `I am a minor` THEN LIST `my parent with whom I live or who has custody of me, or my guardian`, `the Court`
            WHEN `I am incapable of managing my own affairs` THEN LIST `a person with power by law to consent for me`, `the Court`
            WHEN `the trustee cannot find me or does not know whether I am alive` THEN LIST `the Court`

-- s 31(1): the appropriation is made "as to the trustee may seem just and reasonable ...: Provided that -- (a) the
-- appropriation shall not be made so as to affect prejudicially any specific gift; (b) if any consent is required by this
-- section the appropriation shall be made with such consent". Either fails: JUST FALSE ("shall not", "shall").
GIVEN `it would prejudice a specific gift`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `a consent is needed`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent has been given`                IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) -- the trustee may appropriate the property to my share` `it would prejudice a specific gift` `a consent is needed` `the consent has been given` MEANS
    IF `it would prejudice a specific gift`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a consent is needed` AND (NOT `the consent has been given`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part II Division 2 -- notice to claimants (s 33)`

-- s 33(1)(a): notice by advertisement "requiring any person interested to send ... within the time not being less than
-- two months, fixed in the notice or where more than one notice is given, in the last of the notices, particulars of his
-- claim". (3): "At the expiration of the time fixed by the notice the trustees or personal representatives may convey or
-- distribute the property ..., having regard only to the claims ... of which [they] then had notice, and shall not, as
-- respects the property so conveyed or distributed, be liable to any person of whose claim [they] have not had notice at
-- the time of conveyance or distribution". JUST TRUE: s 33 shields them from my claim; JUST FALSE: it does not on these
-- facts (a period the text fixes; "at the expiration"; "not had notice").
GIVEN `the day of the last notice`                IS A DATE
      `the day the notice fixes for claims`       IS A DATE
      `the day of the distribution`               IS A DATE
      `the notices were advertised as section 33 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they had notice of my claim when they distributed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33 -- the trustee is shielded from my claim` `the day of the last notice` `the day the notice fixes for claims` `the day of the distribution` `the notices were advertised as section 33 requires` `they had notice of my claim when they distributed` MEANS
    IF     `the notices were advertised as section 33 requires`
       AND (NOT (`the day the notice fixes for claims` `is before` (`the date` 2 `months after` `the day of the last notice`)))
       AND `the day of the distribution` `is after` `the day the notice fixes for claims`
       AND (NOT `they had notice of my claim when they distributed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part II Division 3 -- maintenance from income during a minority (s 37)`

-- s 37(5): "This section shall not apply where the instrument (if any) under which the interest arises came into
-- operation before the commencement of this Act". The Act came into operation on 1 April 1959 (endnote 1; not in the
-- operative text).
`the day the Act came into operation` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 4 1959

-- Whether s 37 can apply to the interest at all: s 37(5) (instrument before 1 April 1959), s 37(3) ("This section shall
-- apply in the case of a contingent interest only if the limitation or trust carries the intermediate income"), s 2(3)
-- (contrary intention).
GIVEN `the day the instrument came into operation`  IS A DATE
      `my interest is contingent`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift carries the intermediate income`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument expresses a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37 -- the section can apply to my interest` `the day the instrument came into operation` `my interest is contingent` `the gift carries the intermediate income` `the instrument expresses a contrary intention` IF
        (NOT (`the day the instrument came into operation` `is before` `the day the Act came into operation`))
    AND ((NOT `my interest is contingent`) OR `the gift carries the intermediate income`)
    AND (NOT `the instrument expresses a contrary intention`)

-- s 37(1)(a): "during the minority of any such person, if his interest so long continues, the trustees may, at their
-- sole discretion, pay to his parent or guardian (if any) or otherwise apply for or towards his maintenance, education,
-- advancement, or benefit, the whole or such part (if any) of the income of that property as may in all the
-- circumstances be reasonable". Not a minor (a period the text fixes), interest ended ("if"), s 37 cannot apply: JUST
-- FALSE.
GIVEN `my day of birth`                             IS A DATE
      `today`                                       IS A DATE
      `my interest continues`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 37 can apply`                              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(1)(a) -- the trustees may use the income for my maintenance` `my day of birth` `today` `my interest continues` `s 37 can apply` MEANS
    IF `s 37 can apply` AND `my interest continues` AND (NOT (`a person born on` `my day of birth` `has attained` 18 `by` `today`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 37(1)(b): "if such person on attaining the age of eighteen years has not a vested interest in such income, the
-- trustees shall thenceforth pay the income of that property and of any accretion thereto ... to him, until he either
-- attains a vested interest therein or dies, or until failure of his interest". Under 18, or a vested interest in the
-- income (then the gift itself pays it), or the interest failed: JUST FALSE ("if", "thenceforth", "until").
GIVEN `my day of birth`                             IS A DATE
      `today`                                       IS A DATE
      `I have a vested interest in the income`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interest has failed`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 37 can apply`                              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(1)(b) -- the trustees must pay me the income` `my day of birth` `today` `I have a vested interest in the income` `my interest has failed` `s 37 can apply` MEANS
    IF     `s 37 can apply`
       AND `a person born on` `my day of birth` `has attained` 18 `by` `today`
       AND (NOT `I have a vested interest in the income`)
       AND (NOT `my interest has failed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 37(2): the surplus income accumulated during the minority. "(a) If any such person -- (i) attains the age of eighteen
-- years, or marries under that age, and his interest in such income during his minority or until his marriage is a vested
-- interest; or (ii) on attaining the age of eighteen years or on marriage under that age becomes entitled to the property
-- from which such income arose in fee-simple, absolute or determinable, or absolutely, or for an entailed interest -- the
-- trustees shall hold the accumulations in trust for such person absolutely ...; and (b) In any other case the trustees
-- shall ... hold the accumulations as an accretion to the capital of the property ...".
DECLARE `What becomes of the accumulations` IS ONE OF
    `they are still being accumulated, and the trustees may apply them as income meanwhile`
    `they are held in trust for me absolutely`
    `they are added to the capital of the property`

GIVEN `my day of birth`                                    IS A DATE
      `today`                                              IS A DATE
      `I married under 18`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interest in the income during my minority was vested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I became entitled to the property itself absolutely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 37 can apply`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `What becomes of the accumulations`
`s 37(2) -- what becomes of the accumulated income` `my day of birth` `today` `I married under 18` `my interest in the income during my minority was vested` `I became entitled to the property itself absolutely` `s 37 can apply` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 37 can apply`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT (`a person born on` `my day of birth` `has attained` 18 `by` `today`)) AND (NOT `I married under 18`)
         THEN JUST `they are still being accumulated, and the trustees may apply them as income meanwhile`
         ELSE IF `my interest in the income during my minority was vested` OR `I became entitled to the property itself absolutely`
              THEN JUST `they are held in trust for me absolutely`
              ELSE JUST `they are added to the capital of the property`

-- s 37(3): it "applies to a future or contingent legacy by the parent of, or a person standing in loco parentis to, the
-- legatee, if and for such period as, under the general law, the legacy carries interest for the maintenance of the
-- legatee, and in any such case ... the rate of interest shall (if the income available is sufficient, and subject to any
-- rules of court to the contrary) be Five per centum per annum." Outside that case: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own
-- wording* (or *points outside the text*: the general law, the rules of court).
GIVEN `the legacy`                                         IS A NUMBER
      `it is left by my parent or a person in loco parentis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the general law it carries interest for my maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income available is sufficient`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `rules of court set another rate`                    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 37(3) -- the yearly interest my legacy carries` `the legacy` `it is left by my parent or a person in loco parentis` `under the general law it carries interest for my maintenance` `the income available is sufficient` `rules of court set another rate` MEANS
    IF     `it is left by my parent or a person in loco parentis`
       AND `under the general law it carries interest for my maintenance`
       AND `the income available is sufficient`
       AND (NOT `rules of court set another rate`)
    THEN JUST (`the legacy` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part II Division 3 -- advancement out of capital (s 38)`

-- s 38(1): "Where under a trust a person is entitled to the capital of the trust property or any share thereof, the
-- trustees ... may from time to time out of that capital pay or apply for the maintenance education advancement or
-- benefit of that person, an amount not exceeding in all $2000 or half that capital (whichever is the greater) or with
-- the consent of the Court an amount greater than that amount." (5): "No payment or application pursuant to this section
-- shall be made so as to prejudice any person entitled to any prior life or other prior interest ... unless that person is
-- in existence and of full age and consents in writing".
-- "That capital" is read as the capital before any s 38 payment, and "in all" as the total of every payment (fork F10).
-- The cap cannot exceed the capital itself (finding 6).
GIVEN `the capital of my share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(1) -- the cap without the Court` `the capital of my share` MEANS
    min (max 2000 (`the capital of my share` DIVIDED BY 2)) `the capital of my share`

-- What more may still be paid or applied for me. The Court has consented to more: NOTHING-kind *points outside the text*
-- (the Court sets the amount). A prior interest prejudiced without its holder's written consent: 0 ("No payment ...
-- unless"). Not entitled to the capital: NOTHING (s 38 does not reach the case; "where").
GIVEN `I am entitled to the capital or a share of it`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the capital of my share`                             IS A NUMBER
      `already paid or applied for me under section 38`     IS A NUMBER
      `the Court has consented to a greater amount`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prior interest would be prejudiced`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `its holder exists, is of full age and has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument expresses a contrary intention`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 38 -- how much more of my capital may be advanced` `I am entitled to the capital or a share of it` `the capital of my share` `already paid or applied for me under section 38` `the Court has consented to a greater amount` `a prior interest would be prejudiced` `its holder exists, is of full age and has consented in writing` `the instrument expresses a contrary intention` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am entitled to the capital or a share of it`) OR `the instrument expresses a contrary intention`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a prior interest would be prejudiced` AND (NOT `its holder exists, is of full age and has consented in writing`)
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE IF `the Court has consented to a greater amount`
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST (max 0 (`s 38(1) -- the cap without the Court` `the capital of my share` MINUS `already paid or applied for me under section 38`))

§§ `Part II Division 3 -- protective trusts (s 39)`

-- s 39(1)(a): income on protective trusts is held "upon trust for the principal beneficiary during the trust period or
-- until he ... does or attempts to do or suffers any act or thing, or until any event happens, other than an advance
-- under any statutory or express power, whereby if the said income were payable during the trust period to the principal
-- beneficiary absolutely during that period, he would be deprived of the right to receive the same or any part thereof";
-- (b) then for the maintenance, education, advancement or benefit of "(i) the principal beneficiary and his or her wife or
-- husband (if any), and his or her children or more remote issue (if any); or (ii) if there is no wife or husband or issue
-- ... the principal beneficiary and the persons who would, if he were actually dead, be entitled", as the trustees think
-- fit.
DECLARE `Who the protected income is held for` IS ONE OF
    `for me`
    `at the trustees' discretion for me, my spouse and my children or remoter issue`
    `at the trustees' discretion for me and those who would take if I were dead`
    `the trust period has ended`

GIVEN `the trust period is still running`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `an event has happened that would deprive me of the income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event was only an advance under a power`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a spouse or issue`                     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who the protected income is held for`
`s 39 -- who my protected income is held for` `the trust period is still running` `an event has happened that would deprive me of the income` `the event was only an advance under a power` `I have a spouse or issue` MEANS
    IF NOT `the trust period is still running`
    THEN `the trust period has ended`
    ELSE IF `an event has happened that would deprive me of the income` AND (NOT `the event was only an advance under a power`)
         THEN IF `I have a spouse or issue`
              THEN `at the trustees' discretion for me, my spouse and my children or remoter issue`
              ELSE `at the trustees' discretion for me and those who would take if I were dead`
         ELSE `for me`

§§ `Part III -- appointing and discharging trustees (ss 41, 42, 44)`

-- s 41(1): "Where a trustee is dead, or remains out of Victoria for more than one year without having properly delegated
-- the execution of the trust, or desires to be discharged ..., or refuses or is unfit to act therein, or is incapable of
-- acting therein, or is a minor, then ... (a) the person or persons nominated for the purpose of appointing new trustees
-- by the instrument ...; or (b) if there is no such person or no such person able and willing to act, then the surviving
-- or continuing trustees or trustee for the time being, or the personal representatives of the last surviving or
-- continuing trustee -- may, by writing, appoint one or more other persons". (2): a trustee removed under a power in the
-- instrument is replaced "as if he were dead". (3): a dissolved corporation is "deemed to be ... incapable of acting".
DECLARE `What has happened to my trustee` IS ONE OF
    `died`
    `has been out of Victoria`
    `wants to be discharged`
    `refuses to act`
    `is unfit to act`
    `is incapable of acting`
    `is a minor`
    `was removed under a power in the trust instrument`
    `is a corporation that has been dissolved`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Who may appoint a replacement` IS ONE OF
    `the person nominated in the trust instrument to appoint new trustees`
    `the surviving or continuing trustees, or the personal representatives of the last of them`
    `the continuing trustees, but only with leave of my trustee's guardian or administrator`
    `the continuing trustees, but only with leave of the Court`
    `no one under section 41 (the Court may appoint under section 48)`

-- "more than one year": the day after the first anniversary of leaving (fork F11).
-- s 41(9): "If a person who is a patient within the meaning of the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 is a trustee of
-- property and is entitled in possession to some beneficial interest in the property no appointment of a new trustee in
-- his or her place can be made by the continuing trustee or trustees under this section unless leave has been given --
-- (a) in the case of a represented person within the meaning of the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019, by the
-- guardian or administrator; or (b) in any other case, by the Court."
GIVEN `what happened`                                IS A `What has happened to my trustee`
      `the day my trustee left Victoria`             IS A DATE
      `today`                                        IS A DATE
      `my trustee properly delegated the trust`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `a nominated person is able and willing to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my trustee is a patient with a beneficial interest in possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my trustee is a represented person`           IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who may appoint a replacement`
`s 41 -- who may appoint a replacement trustee` `what happened` `the day my trustee left Victoria` `today` `my trustee properly delegated the trust` `a nominated person is able and willing to act` `my trustee is a patient with a beneficial interest in possession` `my trustee is a represented person` MEANS
    IF NOT `there is a ground`
    THEN `no one under section 41 (the Court may appoint under section 48)`
    ELSE IF `a nominated person is able and willing to act`
         THEN `the person nominated in the trust instrument to appoint new trustees`
         ELSE IF `my trustee is a patient with a beneficial interest in possession`
              THEN IF `my trustee is a represented person`
                   THEN `the continuing trustees, but only with leave of my trustee's guardian or administrator`
                   ELSE `the continuing trustees, but only with leave of the Court`
              ELSE `the surviving or continuing trustees, or the personal representatives of the last of them`
    WHERE
        `there is a ground` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what happened`
            WHEN `has been out of Victoria` THEN
                    `today` `is after` (`the date` 12 `months after` `the day my trustee left Victoria`)
                AND (NOT `my trustee properly delegated the trust`)
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 41(6): "Where in the case of any trust, there are not more than three trustees (none of them being a trustee company)
-- ... [the nominated person or the trustees] may, by writing, appoint another person or other persons to be an additional
-- trustee ..., nor shall the number of trustees be increased beyond four by virtue of any such appointment." More than
-- three, a trustee company, or beyond four: JUST FALSE ("where", "shall not").
GIVEN `the number of trustees now`           IS A NUMBER
      `one of them is a trustee company`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number to be added`               IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(6) -- additional trustees may be appointed` `the number of trustees now` `one of them is a trustee company` `the number to be added` MEANS
    IF     `the number of trustees now` AT MOST 3
       AND (NOT `one of them is a trustee company`)
       AND (`the number of trustees now` PLUS `the number to be added`) AT MOST 4
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 44(1): "This section applies where a trustee declares by writing that he is desirous of being discharged ..., and
-- after his discharge there will be either a trustee company or at least two individuals to act as trustees". (2): "if
-- the co-trustees and such other person (if any) as is empowered to appoint trustees consent by writing to the discharge
-- ..., the trustee ... (b) subject to subsection (3) ..., shall ... be discharged". (3): "the retiring trustee shall not be
-- discharged until [any part needing a conveyance] is duly conveyed." (s 42(1)(c) says the same of a discharge on a new
-- appointment.) Any of these unmet: JUST FALSE ("where", "if", "until").
GIVEN `my trustee has declared in writing a wish to be discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `individuals who will remain as trustees`                   IS A NUMBER
      `a trustee company will remain as trustee`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the co-trustees and any appointor have consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every conveyance needed has been made`                     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 -- my trustee is discharged without a replacement` `my trustee has declared in writing a wish to be discharged` `individuals who will remain as trustees` `a trustee company will remain as trustee` `the co-trustees and any appointor have consented in writing` `every conveyance needed has been made` MEANS
    IF     `my trustee has declared in writing a wish to be discharged`
       AND (`a trustee company will remain as trustee` OR `individuals who will remain as trustees` AT LEAST 2)
       AND `the co-trustees and any appointor have consented in writing`
       AND `every conveyance needed has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part IV -- the Court's powers on a beneficiary's application (ss 48, 51, 55, 63, 63A, 64, 67, 68, 69)`

-- s 64(1): "An order under this Act for the appointment of a new trustee or concerning any property, subject to a trust,
-- may be made on the application of any person beneficially interested in the property, whether under disability or
-- not, or on the application of any person duly appointed trustee thereof." Not beneficially interested: NOTHING-kind
-- *silent* (the list is not closed with "only"; the applicant would have to rely on something else).
--
-- s 48(1): "The Court may, whenever it is expedient to appoint a new trustee or new trustees, and it is found inexpedient
-- difficult or impracticable so to do without the assistance of the Court, make an order appointing a new trustee ...
-- In particular ... the Court may make an order appointing a new trustee in substitution for a trustee who is convicted
-- on indictment of any offence, or is a patient within the meaning of the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022, or is a
-- bankrupt, or is a corporation which is in liquidation or has been dissolved." Neither: JUST FALSE ("whenever", ruling
-- (c); fork F12).
DECLARE `Particular ground for the Court` IS ONE OF
    `my trustee has been convicted on indictment`
    `my trustee is a patient under the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`
    `my trustee is bankrupt`
    `my trustee is a corporation in liquidation or dissolved`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `I am beneficially interested`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particular ground`                             IS A `Particular ground for the Court`
      `it is expedient and impracticable without the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 48, 64 -- the Court may appoint a new trustee on my application` `I am beneficially interested` `the particular ground` `it is expedient and impracticable without the Court` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am beneficially interested`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it is expedient and impracticable without the Court` OR (NOT (`the particular ground` EQUALS `none of these`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 51(2): "A vesting order may be made in any of the following cases ... (i) where a trustee neglects or refuses to
-- convey any property, or to receive the dividends or income of any property, or to sue for or recover any property
-- according to the direction of the person absolutely entitled to the same for twenty-eight days next after a request in
-- writing has been made to him by the person so entitled".
-- Encoded as a regulative rule: the trustee MUST act as directed WITHIN 28 days of the written request, LEST the case for
-- a vesting order arises. The request day is day 0; acting on day 28 is in time; from day 29 the case is open (fork F13).
DECLARE `Trust party` IS ONE OF
    `the trustee`

DECLARE `Trustee act` IS ONE OF
    `review the performance of the trust investments`
    `convey, receive or sue as the person absolutely entitled directed`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Trust party` `Trustee act`
`s 51(2)(i) -- the trustee must act on the written request` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the trustee`
    MUST `convey, receive or sue as the person absolutely entitled directed`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the trustee` BECAUSE "the trustee neglected or refused for twenty-eight days after the written request of the person absolutely entitled; the Court may make a vesting order (s 51(2)(i))"

-- s 6(3): "Subject to the instrument creating the trust, a trustee must, at least once in each year, review the
-- performance (individually and as a whole) of trust investments." Read as: within one year of the last review (or of
-- the first investment), the anniversary itself in time (fork F2).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Trust party` `Trustee act`
`s 6(3) -- the investments must be reviewed within the year` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the trustee`
    MUST `review the performance of the trust investments`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the trustee` BECAUSE "the trustee did not review the performance of the trust investments at least once in the year (s 6(3))"

-- The helper that runs a duty over what happened (in the shape of the Civil Procedure Act 2010 encoding's helper). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED means in time
-- and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in time. It takes a
-- DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`

GIVEN `the rule`                    IS A DEONTIC `Trust party` `Trustee act`
      `the act`                     IS A `Trustee act`
      `the act has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of the trustee's duty` `the rule` `the act` `the act has been done` `the time the act was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the trustee` `the act` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the trustee` `the act` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

DECLARE `What my written request led to` IS ONE OF
    `the trustee acted within the 28 days`
    `the 28 days are still running`
    `the trustee neglected for 28 days: the Court may make a vesting order`

GIVEN `I am absolutely entitled to the property`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of my written request`              IS A DATE
      `the trustee has acted as I directed`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the trustee acted`                  IS A DATE
      `today`                                      IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `What my written request led to`
`s 51(2)(i) -- what my written request led to` `I am absolutely entitled to the property` `the day of my written request` `the trustee has acted as I directed` `the day the trustee acted` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am absolutely entitled to the property`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `what became of the trustee's duty` (`s 51(2)(i) -- the trustee must act on the written request` 28) `convey, receive or sue as the person absolutely entitled directed` `the trustee has acted as I directed` (`the days from` `the day of my written request` `to` `the day the trustee acted`) (`the days from` `the day of my written request` `to` `today`)
         WHEN `done in time` THEN JUST `the trustee acted within the 28 days`
         WHEN `still open` THEN JUST `the 28 days are still running`
         WHEN `not done in time` THEN JUST `the trustee neglected for 28 days: the Court may make a vesting order`

-- s 6(3) run over the facts: from the day of the last review (or of the first investment) to the same day a year later.
-- The instrument provides otherwise: NOTHING-kind *points outside the text*.
GIVEN `the day of the last review`              IS A DATE
      `the trustee has reviewed since`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the next review`              IS A DATE
      `today`                                   IS A DATE
      `the instrument provides otherwise`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `What became of the duty`
`s 6(3) -- what became of the yearly review` `the day of the last review` `the trustee has reviewed since` `the day of the next review` `today` `the instrument provides otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the instrument provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`what became of the trustee's duty` (`s 6(3) -- the investments must be reviewed within the year` (`the days from` `the day of the last review` `to` (`the date` 12 `months after` `the day of the last review`))) `review the performance of the trust investments` `the trustee has reviewed since` (`the days from` `the day of the last review` `to` `the day of the next review`) (`the days from` `the day of the last review` `to` `today`))

-- s 55: "Where a minor is beneficially entitled to any property the Court may, with a view to the application of the
-- capital or income thereof for the maintenance, education, advancement or benefit of the minor, make an order -- (a)
-- appointing a person to convey such property; or (b) in the case of stock, or a thing in action, vesting in any person the
-- right to transfer ... or to receive the dividends or income thereof, or to sue for and recover such thing in action".
-- Not a minor, or not beneficially entitled: JUST FALSE ("where").
GIVEN `my day of birth`                 IS A DATE
      `today`                           IS A DATE
      `I am beneficially entitled to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55 -- the Court may make an order so my property can be used for me` `my day of birth` `today` `I am beneficially entitled to the property` MEANS
    IF `I am beneficially entitled to the property` AND (NOT (`a person born on` `my day of birth` `has attained` 18 `by` `today`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 63(1): "Where in the management or administration of any property vested in trustees, any sale, lease, mortgage,
-- surrender, release or other disposition, or any purchase, investment, acquisition, expenditure or other transaction, is
-- in the opinion of the Court expedient, but the same cannot be effected by reason of the absence of any power for that
-- purpose vested in the trustees by the trust instrument (if any) or by law, the Court may by order confer upon the
-- trustees ... the necessary power". (3): "An application ... may be made by the trustees, or by any of them, or by any
-- person beneficially interested under the trust." The trustees already have the power, or the Court does not find it
-- expedient: JUST FALSE ("where"). Not beneficially interested: NOTHING-kind *silent*.
GIVEN `I am beneficially interested`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees lack the power`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court finds the transaction expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63 -- the Court may give the trustees the power on my application` `I am beneficially interested` `the trustees lack the power` `the Court finds the transaction expedient` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am beneficially interested`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the trustees lack the power` AND `the Court finds the transaction expedient`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 63A(1): "the Court may if it thinks fit by order approve on behalf of -- (a) any person having ... an interest ...
-- who by reason of minority or other incapacity is incapable of assenting; or (b) any person ... who may become entitled
-- ... as being at a future date or on the happening of a future event a person of any specified description or a member
-- of any specified class of persons, so however that this paragraph shall not include any person who would be of that
-- description, or a member of that class ... if the said date had fallen or the said event had happened at the date of the
-- application to the Court; or (c) any person unborn; or (d) any person in respect of any discretionary interest of his
-- under protective trusts where the interest of the principal beneficiary has not failed or determined -- any arrangement
-- ... varying or revoking all or any of the trusts, or enlarging the powers of the trustees ...: Provided that except by
-- virtue of paragraph (d) ... the Court shall not approve an arrangement on behalf of any person unless the carrying out
-- thereof would be for the benefit of that person." (4): "Nothing ... shall apply to trusts affecting property settled
-- by Act of Parliament."
DECLARE `Why the Court would approve for me` IS ONE OF
    `(a) I am a minor or otherwise incapable of assenting`
    `(b) I may become entitled later as one of a described class`
    `(b) I would already be in that class if the date or event had happened at the application`
    `(c) I am not yet born`
    `(d) I have a discretionary interest under a protective trust that has not failed`
    `I am an adult able to assent for myself`

GIVEN `why`                                       IS A `Why the Court would approve for me`
      `the arrangement would benefit me`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property was settled by Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A -- the Court may approve the variation on my behalf` `why` `the arrangement would benefit me` `the property was settled by Act of Parliament` MEANS
    IF `the property was settled by Act of Parliament`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `why`
         WHEN `(d) I have a discretionary interest under a protective trust that has not failed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `(b) I would already be in that class if the date or event had happened at the application` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `I am an adult able to assent for myself` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE
            IF `the arrangement would benefit me`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 67: "If it appears to the Court that a trustee ... is or may be personally liable for any breach of trust ..., but
-- has acted honestly and reasonably, and ought fairly to be excused for the breach of trust and for omitting to obtain the
-- directions of the Court ..., then the Court may relieve him either wholly or partly from personal liability". Any
-- unmet: JUST FALSE ("if").
GIVEN `my trustee acted honestly`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `my trustee acted reasonably`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `my trustee ought fairly to be excused`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67 -- the Court may relieve my trustee from personal liability` `my trustee acted honestly` `my trustee acted reasonably` `my trustee ought fairly to be excused` MEANS
    IF `my trustee acted honestly` AND `my trustee acted reasonably` AND `my trustee ought fairly to be excused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 68: "Where a trustee commits a breach of trust at the instigation or request or with the consent in writing of a
-- beneficiary the Court may, if it thinks fit, ... make such order as to the Court seems just for impounding all or any
-- part of the interest of the beneficiary in the trust estate by way of indemnity to the trustee". A consent not in
-- writing and no instigation or request: JUST FALSE ("where").
GIVEN `I instigated the breach`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `I requested the breach`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `I consented to the breach in writing`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68 -- the Court may impound my interest to indemnify the trustee` `I instigated the breach` `I requested the breach` `I consented to the breach in writing` MEANS
    IF `I instigated the breach` OR `I requested the breach` OR `I consented to the breach in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 69(1): "Trustees or the majority of trustees having in their hands or under their control money or securities
-- subject to a trust may pay the same into court"; (3): where "the majority are desirous of paying the same into court,
-- but the concurrence of the other or others cannot be obtained, the Court may order the payment into court to be made by
-- the majority without the concurrence of the other or others"; (7): "Court means the Supreme Court".
DECLARE `How the money may go into court` IS ONE OF
    `the trustees may pay it into the Supreme Court`
    `the majority may pay it into the Supreme Court, the others concurring`
    `the majority may ask the Supreme Court to order payment in without the others`

GIVEN `the number of trustees`                    IS A NUMBER
      `the number who want to pay it into court`  IS A NUMBER
      `the others concur`                         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `How the money may go into court`
`s 69 -- how the trust money may be paid into court` `the number of trustees` `the number who want to pay it into court` `the others concur` MEANS
    IF `the number who want to pay it into court` AT LEAST `the number of trustees`
    THEN JUST `the trustees may pay it into the Supreme Court`
    ELSE IF (`the number who want to pay it into court` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `the number of trustees`
         THEN IF `the others concur`
              THEN JUST `the majority may pay it into the Supreme Court, the others concurring`
              ELSE JUST `the majority may ask the Supreme Court to order payment in without the others`
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part V -- commission (s 77)`

-- s 77: "It shall be lawful for the Court or an Associate Judge of the Court to allow out of the trust funds to the
-- trustee of a settlement such commission or percentage not exceeding five per centum for his pains and trouble as is just
-- and reasonable." What the five per cent is reckoned on is not stated (finding 7): an input. Not the trustee of a
-- settlement: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*.
GIVEN `my trustee is the trustee of a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum the commission is reckoned on`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 77 -- the most commission the Court may allow` `my trustee is the trustee of a settlement` `the sum the commission is reckoned on` MEANS
    IF `my trustee is the trustee of a settlement`
    THEN JUST (`the sum the commission is reckoned on` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE NOTHING
